+# Dense full-suite evaluation queue implementation plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** Use superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task.
+
+**Goal:** Append full-suite Dense-S12 then Dense-S30 to the current v0 evaluation campaign.
+**Architecture:** Independent pinned worktree and dependent controller wait for all five v0 conditions to finish. Adapt the audited matched rollout runner without changing any active v0 files. Each Dense model keeps its native one-pass architecture.
+**Tech Stack:** Python, PyTorch, LIBERO, tmux, Hugging Face pinned HTTPS downloads.
+**Spec:** User's two full-suite checkpoint URLs; inherited standard LIBERO protocol.
+
+## Global constraints
+- NFE10; seeds42,43,44; four suites; ten tasks/suite;50 episodes/task/seed;6000/model.
+- No GPU work until v0 finishes; do not change active source or interrupt other GPU users.
+- Verify download size, SHA256/LFS and Git blob hashes, full-scope epoch10 metadata and strict state dict.
+- Original normalization, text, VAE, images, settling30, predict32/execute10, caps400/700.
+- CUDA graph requires bit-exact real-observation and rollout parity; choose measured fastest safe worker count.
+- Preserve query traces, every video, resumable whole groups, atomic reports and fail-closed provenance.
+
+## Review focus
+- Missing/failed predecessor must never unlock Dense GPU jobs.
+- Dense architecture must never receive a v0 Ka override.
+- Dense-S30 memory headroom, fallback and resume consistency.
+- Wrong checkpoint/suite/seed/episode identity must fail accounting.
+- Frozen source and assets must include all new controllers and model-specific metadata.
+
+## Tasks
+- [ ] Download both revision-pinned releases, verify all objects and CPU checkpoint contracts.
+- [ ] Adapt dense_common/runner/gate/queue; implement dense_chain waiting for v0 completion and lock release.
+- [ ] Test dependency gating, model identities, episode accounting and profile selection; run CPU strict model loads.
+- [ ] Obtain independent review, address findings, freeze source, launch tmux waiter and verify status/report.
+
+## Execution decisions
+Proceed inline under the user's explicit request to append and run. A separate dependent queue is necessary because the active v0 queue freezes its source. GPU correctness/performance gates run automatically after the predecessor; CPU release checks run now.
